 2>&1 | tail -2; diff /tmp/outline8.md story-wiki/Outline.md"]], "output": "```console\n85c85\n<   - **Floor b by B (K=10 independent backgrounds, same instances as floor a; `floor_b_by_background.csv`):** median top-3 agreement B20 0.46, B50 0.62, B200 0.75, k-means-50 0.72. So the background-draw part shrinks with B, as idea-review expected, and a part of the reference's instability (the choice of reference distribution: k-means 0.72 < B200 is not a draw effect) remains. Against the shap default at the default budget floor b is below floor a in 24 of 24 rows (68 of 68 largest-sampled rows), but **against paired Kernel at the same budget the sign is mixed** (13 of 24 positive, 7 with CI above 0). The co-headline is therefore stated for *shap's default estimator at B=50*, with the B curve; \"the value function, not the run, dominates\" is not stated for paired Kernel SHAP or as a general claim. Pending rows: German/ACS-Employment/GMSC MLP (n=10, K=6) are absent, and the run-level share P_c ≥ 0.9 at default is background-invariant (1.0 under every background).\n---\n>   - **Floor b by B (K=10 independent backgrounds, same instances as floor a; `floor_b_by_background.csv`):** median top-3 agreement B20 0.46, B50 0.61, B200 0.75, k-means-50 0.77 over 18 cells (rev 9: current CSV, with GMSC MLP; the 0.62/0.72 I quoted in rev 8 were from the earlier delivery). So the background-draw part shrinks with B, as idea-review expected, and a part of the reference's instability (the choice of reference distribution: k-means-50 is not above B200 only by chance: reference-distribution choice is a separate entry) remains. Against the shap default at the default budget floor b is below floor a in 24 of 24 rows (68 of 68 largest-sampled rows), but **against paired Kernel at the same budget the sign is mixed** (13 of 24 rows positive, 7 with CI above 0 at the earlier delivery; with GMSC MLP, 7 of 13 non-linear cells exclude zero, 5 background floor higher, 2 lower). The co-headline is therefore stated for *shap's default estimator at B=50*, with the B curve; \"the value function, not the run, dominates\" is not stated for paired Kernel SHAP or as a general claim. Pending rows: German/ACS-Employment/GMSC MLP (n=10, K=6) are absent, and the run-level share P_c ≥ 0.9 at default is background-invariant (1.0 under every background).\n106a107\n> - rev 9: numbers of floor b by B updated to the current CSV (B50 0.61, k-means 0.77); `paper-repo` applied rev 8 (issue #6 closed).\n```", "exit": null}}}, {"id": "97e97062-7a7d-5b09-a7ea-e008891f1f6d", "at": 1795645875.0478854, "clock": "host", "stream": "runner", "sequence": 63659, "layer": "worker", "category": "message", "kind": "session.session/request_permission", "role": "idea-review-repo", "actor": "idea-review-repo", "execution_id": "cfb22e446b7418e6c90198fcc154d407", "trust": "agent-reported", "outcome": null, "label": "message", "repository": null, "flags": [], "causes": [], "summary": "session/request_permission"}, {"id": "11f4a504-9d7d-5cdd-8c88-ab4ad35723ed", "at": 1795645875.0525966, "clock": "host", "stream": "runner", "sequence": 63660, "layer": "worker", "category": "message", "kind": "session.response", "role": "idea-review-repo", "actor": "idea-review-repo", "execution_id": "cfb22e446b7418e6c90198fcc154d407", "trust": "agent-reported", "outcome": null, "label": "message", "repository": null, "flags": [], "causes": [], "summary": "response"}, {"id": "3992133c-baaf-5788-a4f3-bc264b4dbc81", "at": 1795645875.054812, "clock": "host", "stream": "runner", "sequence": 63661, "layer": "worker", "category": "usage", "kind": "session.usage", "role": "idea-review-repo", "actor": "idea-review-repo", "execution_id": "cfb22e446b7418e6c90198fcc154d407", "trust": "agent-reported", "outcome": null, "label": "usage", "repository": null, "flags": [], "causes": [], "summary": "context usage"}, {"id": "7e37bc78-e9d2-516e-b00f-91b4ae979a5e", "at": 1795645875.5568118, "clock": "host", "stream": "runner", "sequence"